    "title": "Homestead man charged with drug trafficking - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff Writer ,\n7 hours ago\nMARATHON — A 49-year-old Homestead man was arrested Wednesday, Sept. 10, following a traffic stop on U.S. 1 in which more than 2 ounces of cocaine were allegedly found.\nTravis Bernard Holton was charged with trafficking in cocaine, according to the Monroe County Sheriff's Office.\nDeputies stopped a Chevrolet sedan near mile marker 56 at 7:42 p.m. for a traffic infraction. K9 Mako alerted to drugs in the vehicle and 61.29 grams in powder and crack cocaine were subsequently found, reports say.\nHolton was taken to jail.",
